{"slug":"yvette-clarke","qid":"Q461679","name":"Yvette Clarke","desc":"American politician (born 1964)","article":"Yvette Clarke","born":"1964-11-21","died":null,"birthplace":"New York City","parties":["Democratic Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-09","f":2013,"u":null},{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"NY-11","f":2007,"u":2013}],"summary":"Yvette Diane Clarke (born November 21, 1964) is an American politician representing New York's 9th congressional district in the U.S. House of Representatives. First elected  to Congress in 2006, she initially represented New York's 11th congressional district from 2007 to 2013, before transitioning to the 9th district following redistricting. Previously, Clarke represented the 40th district in Brooklyn on the New York City Council from 2002 to 2006.","photo":{"f":"yvette-clarke.jpg","by":"Brian Thorpe","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2026_Official_Portrait_of_Rep._Clarke_(D-NY).jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","n":"Yvette Clarke","race":"NY-09"},{"y":2024,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":173207,"s":73.46,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D. Clarke"},{"y":2022,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":116970,"s":81.31,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2020,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":230221,"s":83.04,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2018,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":181455,"s":89.2,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2016,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":214189,"s":92.29,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2014,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":82659,"s":89.47,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"NY-09","p":"D","v":186141,"s":87.27,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"NY-11","p":"D","v":104297,"s":90.57,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"NY-11","p":"D","v":168562,"s":92.76,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"NY-11","p":"D","v":88334,"s":90.04,"w":true,"n":"Yvette D Clarke"}]}